Z||000000||Rumor||12-17-2001||12:36 AM||||Howdy again!<P>I have an 85 GT.<BR>  My oil pressure is very close to the red zone - like 25/80. The oil was changed less then a month ago, and it is past the "full" mark on the dipstick (I tested it after driving for about 20 minutes, and wiped it before I read it)  Any ideas why it is so low? I have noticed that it will sometimes go up higher when I am accelerating.  Thanks for any info you may have!<P>-Rumor||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-17-2001||12:47 AM||||how many miles are on the engine?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rumor||12-17-2001||06:46 AM||||96k.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-17-2001||10:38 AM||||are u saying you have 25 pnds idle, and 80 driving? Is you oil 'over' full mark or low? anything over 10-15 pnds is safe at idle. Normal driving should be between 30-60 pnds. If your oil is low, how many miles have you driven since you last put any in? Also if you 'overfill' oil, it will blow out, possibly taking a seal with it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BigTurbo87GT||12-17-2001||11:19 AM||||Probably just got worn rod and/or main bearings.<BR>Pretty normal for 100k'ish miles on a 2.8 (the way Fiero's get driven anyway).<BR>I replaced the bearings and oil pump @ 134K in my 87GT. Fixed it right up (didn't even need any machine work to the crank!). Before I changed the bearings, I had almost normal pressure above 1500 rpm (still lower than spec though) but at idle it was 10lbs or less (less after warming up, oh and don't trust the dash guage, use a mechanical guage to verify pressure).<BR>After the bearings and a high volume oil pump I ran about 65lbs of pressure off idle and about 40 @ idle (as I recall, it's been a while now), which is more than necessary but I ran the holy piss out of that motor :-D.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lou_dias||12-17-2001||12:06 PM||||wrong oil filter||||reg||1
Z||000006||Scotty||12-17-2001||12:28 PM||||Don't forget them pesky cam bearings! But it seems usual that my GT runs with about 20 at idle. ||||reg||1
